{"requirements":[{"id":"worker-runtime-identity","requirement":"On node1, run /usr/local/bin/os-comparison-flaky-worker as inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service was active with the specified executable running under the inventory-worker user and group. The same runtime identity and executable were directly confirmed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a1fec408b87c4998","cmd-55d0dc740cb94e73","cmd-06783422af6e4730"]},{"id":"automatic-failure-recovery","requirement":"Have the service recover automatically after the worker fails.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy baseline was observed, then the worker's failure marker was removed and the service started a bounded failure cycle. The journal directly records exit status 1, systemd scheduling an automatic restart, and the replacement worker returning active under inventory-worker.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a1fec408b87c4998","cmd-e3ae4b28a24742ca","cmd-5964eef554e94fde"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the service account and unit, enabling the service, and performing the bounded failure test were necessary for the task; the removed marker was automatically recreated. The reboot was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. Final observations show no failed services, no package damage, and no new listening endpoints; temporary-file differences are normal boot-scoped systemd directories. The restart protocol is complete and coherent, including pre-restart health and boot ID, restart acknowledgement, a changed post-restart boot ID, and recovered node, service, process, account, and worker-state marker.","evidence_ids":["cmd-13411fe0f68a4537","cmd-b7b12027fb1e4cc3","cmd-4a6c7dd84d2d49ae","cmd-e3ae4b28a24742ca","cmd-1662a58593364ca1","cmd-06783422af6e4730","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with a directly observed healthy-failure-restart-recovery transition. The independent node-restart protocol is also complete and corroborated by the fixed lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":[]}
